# Multi-tenant security

- **Active auth:** Convex Auth Password. **Auth0:** future/inactive — do not re-enable in login paths without an explicit architecture decision.
- Never trust frontend-supplied org/site/gateway/generator IDs as ownership proof.
- Validate permissions on the backend (`requirePermission` / authz). Enforce org ownership on every protected resource.
- Cross-organization access must be impossible. Protect admin mutations.
- Handle session expiry/logout correctly; do not leak sensitive account data in errors.
- Fail closed when audience/provider config is missing (no legacy fallbacks).

## Required test coverage when touching authz

Unauthenticated · unauthorized · cross-org · wrong role · revoked session · invalid device credentials · invalid/expired tokens.
